 with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Colorado remains a Democratic-leaning state in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of about six points Democratic and no Republican carrying the state at the top of the ticket in two decades. The 2028 race is fully open: the incumbent president is term-limited, so neither party begins with an incumbent advantage.\n\nEarly signals are mixed but modestly favorable to Democrats. National primary polling shows Democratic contenders running well against likely Republican nominees, and one survey found even a progressive matchup ahead of a MAGA-aligned Republican. At the same time, progressive upsets in Colorado's 2026 primaries could reshape the Democratic ticket. With no Colorado general-election polls or expert ratings published yet, the forecast rests on fundamentals and carries unusually wide uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7597, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6966, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7137, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.701, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.713, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7202, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7103, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7097, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7338, "margin": 6.5}]}